    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0541" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/975.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s November 28. The Legation thought that the Department’s November 24,
                    7 p.m., rejected my recommendations of November 22. Consequently I immediately
                    requested of the President all that the Department’s telegram pointed out, and
                    also the publication of a proclamation promising the safeguards named by you.
                    Although the requests have not yet been answered, the Secretary of the Interior
                    has responded with a command to the governors to secure the proper conditions
                    for a fair election.</p>
                <p>I believe that my recommendations of November 22 should be put in force to
                    supplement and fortify your instruction of November 24, <pb facs="0542" n="438"
                        xml:id="pg438"/> 7 p.m. Agents for observation only, in my opinion, would
                    cause least dissatisfaction.</p>
                <p>The Department’s influence is already giving to the people and the press
                    privileges never enjoyed before under similar circumstances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
